_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 19
---
order: 19
---
short_label: XI.19
---
statement: If two planes which cut one another are at right angles to any plane, then their intersection is also at right angles to the same plane.
---
proof:

Let the two planes *AB* and *BC* be at right angles to the plane of reference, and let *BC* be their intersection.

I say that *BD* is at right angles to the plane of reference.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.19 diagram" src="propXI19.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
